    "readout_text": "To determine how many square centimeters of paper Jackson can cover with paint, we need to calculate the area of the strip he can create using the paint.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Shape and Dimensions\n\nJackson's paintbrush creates a **rectangular strip** of paint. The area of a rectangle is given by:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{Length} \\times \\text{Width}\n$$\n\nWe are given:\n- **Width** = 6.5 millimeters\n- **Length** = 25 meters\n\nSince the final answer is required in **square centimeters**, we need to convert both measurements to centimeters.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Convert Units\n\n- **Width**:  \n  $$\n  6.5 \\text{ mm} = \\frac{6.5}{10} = 0.65 \\text{ cm}\n  $$\n\n- **Length**:  \n  $$\n  25 \\text{ m} = 25 \\times 100 = 2500 \\text{ cm}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the Area\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{Length} \\times \\text{Width} = 2500 \\text{ cm} \\times 0.65 \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = 1625 \\text{ cm}^2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{1625}\n$$\n\nJackson can cover **1625 square centimeters** of paper with paint.",
